   "source": [
    "# 02b · Regresión Logística Clínica — OR Ajustados\n",
    "**Proyecto:** Predicción de Hospitalización por Dengue — Bucaramanga  \n",
    "**Fase:** Análisis multivariado explicativo  \n",
    "**Origen:** `DengueConSignosTodosSintomas.ipynb` — secciones de regresión logística\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Propósito\n",
    "\n",
    "Este notebook construye modelos de **regresión logística interpretable** (statsmodels)\n",
    "para identificar las manifestaciones clínicas con asociación **independiente** con\n",
    "la hospitalización, controlando por confusores.\n",
    "\n",
    "Se comparan cuatro modelos anidados:\n",
    "1. **M1:** Solo signos de alarma\n",
    "2. **M2:** Signos de alarma + síntomas generales (todas las clínicas)\n",
    "3. **M3:** M1 + variables sociodemográficas\n",
    "4. **M4:** M2 + variables sociodemográficas (modelo completo)\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Distinción clave:** La regresión logística con statsmodels es un modelo **explicativo**\n",
    "> (objetivo: cuantificar asociaciones y calcular OR con IC95%) y no debe confundirse\n",
    "> con los modelos **predictivos** del notebook 03. Los criterios de evaluación son\n",
    "> distintos: aquí importa el AIC/BIC, pseudo-R², VIF y plausibilidad clínica;\n",
    "> en el notebook 03 importan AUC-ROC, F1-score y calibración.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# IMPORTACIONES\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, \"../../src\")\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.patches as mpatches\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "from scipy.stats import chi2\n",
    "import statsmodels.formula.api as smf\n",
    "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
    "from statsmodels.stats.outliers_influence import variance_inflation_factor\n",
    "\n",
    "import config\n",
    "from config import (\n",
    "    DATA_INTERIM, OUT_FIGURES, OUT_TABLES, CHECKPOINTS,\n",
    "    COLORS, TARGET_COL, SIGNOS_ALARMA, SINTOMAS_GENERALES, VARIABLES_DEMOGRAFICAS\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\n",
    "    \"figure.dpi\": 150, \"savefig.dpi\": 300,\n",
    "    \"figure.facecolor\": \"white\", \"axes.facecolor\": \"white\",\n",
    "    \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n",
    "    \"axes.titlesize\": 14, \"axes.titleweight\": \"bold\",\n",
    "    \"axes.labelsize\": 12,\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "df_con = joblib.load(DATA_INTERIM / \"datos_con_signos.pkl\")\n",
    "df_sin = joblib.load(DATA_INTERIM / \"datos_sin_signos.pkl\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Datos cargados: DCSA {df_con.shape[0]:,} | DSSA {df_sin.shape[0]:,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Preparación de variables"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# PREPARACIÓN DE VARIABLES PARA REGRESIÓN\n",
    "# Las variables clínicas se recodifican: 1=sí, 0=no (era 1/2 en SIVIGILA).\n",
    "# Las variables sociodemográficas se tratan como categóricas (C()) en la\n",
    "# fórmula de statsmodels para generar dummies automáticamente.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "todas_clinicas = SINTOMAS_GENERALES + SIGNOS_ALARMA\n",
    "\n",
    "def preparar_df_regresion(df, variables_clinicas, variables_demo=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Prepara el dataframe para regresión logística.\"\"\"\n",
    "    cols = variables_clinicas + ([TARGET_COL])\n",
    "    if variables_demo:\n",
    "        cols += variables_demo\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_out = df[cols].copy().dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Recodificar clínicas (1=sí, 0=no)\n",
    "    for var in variables_clinicas:\n",
    "        df_out[var] = df_out[var].map({1: 1, 2: 0})\n",
    "\n",
    "    return df_out\n",
    "\n",
    "vars_demo = [\"SEXO_\", \"DEF_CLAS_EDAD\", \"TIP_SS_\", \"ESTRATO_\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_reg_m1 = preparar_df_regresion(df_con, SIGNOS_ALARMA)\n",
    "df_reg_m2 = preparar_df_regresion(df_con, todas_clinicas)\n",
    "df_reg_m3 = preparar_df_regresion(df_con, SIGNOS_ALARMA, vars_demo)\n",
    "df_reg_m4 = preparar_df_regresion(df_con, todas_clinicas, vars_demo)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"M1 (solo signos):  {df_reg_m1.shape[0]:,} obs\")\n",
    "print(f\"M2 (todas clín.):  {df_reg_m2.shape[0]:,} obs\")\n",
    "print(f\"M3 (signos+demo):  {df_reg_m3.shape[0]:,} obs\")\n",
    "print(f\"M4 (completo):     {df_reg_m4.shape[0]:,} obs\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# AJUSTE DE MODELOS LOGÍSTICOS\n",
    "# Se usa statsmodels (no scikit-learn) porque provee:\n",
    "# - Odds Ratios directamente interpretables en el OR = exp(coef)\n",
    "# - Intervalos de confianza al 95% por perfil de verosimilitud\n",
    "# - p-valores de Wald individuales\n",
    "# - AIC, BIC, pseudo-R² de McFadden\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "def construir_formula(target, clinicas, demos=None):\n",
    "    terminos = list(clinicas)\n",
    "    if demos:\n",
    "        terminos += [f\"C({v})\" for v in demos]\n",
    "    return f\"{target} ~ \" + \" + \".join(terminos)\n",
    "\n",
    "formula_m1 = construir_formula(TARGET_COL, SIGNOS_ALARMA)\n",
    "formula_m2 = construir_formula(TARGET_COL, todas_clinicas)\n",
    "formula_m3 = construir_formula(TARGET_COL, SIGNOS_ALARMA, vars_demo)\n",
    "formula_m4 = construir_formula(TARGET_COL, todas_clinicas, vars_demo)\n",
    "\n",
    "modelos = {}\n",
    "for nombre, formula, df_reg in [\n",
    "    (\"M1_signos\",    formula_m1, df_reg_m1),\n",
    "    (\"M2_todas\",     formula_m2, df_reg_m2),\n",
    "    (\"M3_sig_demo\",  formula_m3, df_reg_m3),\n",
    "    (\"M4_completo\",  formula_m4, df_reg_m4),\n",
    "]:\n",
    "    modelos[nombre] = smf.logit(formula=formula, data=df_reg).fit(disp=False)\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ {nombre} ajustado | AIC: {modelos[nombre].aic:.1f} | Pseudo-R²: {modelos[nombre].prsquared:.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Comparación de modelos"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# COMPARACIÓN DE MODELOS ANIDADOS\n",
    "# La prueba de razón de verosimilitudes (Likelihood Ratio Test) evalúa si\n",
    "# la incorporación de variables adicionales mejora significativamente el ajuste.\n",
    "# Hipótesis nula: el modelo reducido ajusta igual que el modelo completo.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "comparacion = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Modelo\": [\"M1: Solo signos\", \"M2: Todas clínicas\",\n",
    "               \"M3: Signos + demo\", \"M4: Completo\"],\n",
    "    \"N_vars\": [int(m.df_model) for m in modelos.values()],\n",
    "    \"Log-Likelihood\": [round(m.llf, 2) for m in modelos.values()],\n",
    "    \"AIC\": [round(m.aic, 2) for m in modelos.values()],\n",
    "    \"BIC\": [round(m.bic, 2) for m in modelos.values()],\n",
    "    \"Pseudo_R2\": [round(m.prsquared, 4) for m in modelos.values()],\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# LRT: M1 vs M2\n",
    "lr_stat_12 = 2 * (modelos[\"M2_todas\"].llf - modelos[\"M1_signos\"].llf)\n",
    "df_diff_12 = modelos[\"M2_todas\"].df_model - modelos[\"M1_signos\"].df_model\n",
    "p_lr_12 = chi2.sf(lr_stat_12, df_diff_12)\n",
    "\n",
    "display(comparacion)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nLRT M1 vs M2: LR={lr_stat_12:.2f}, df={df_diff_12:.0f}, p={p_lr_12:.2e}\")\n",
    "print(\"→ Los síntomas generales aportan información adicional significativa\" if p_lr_12 < 0.05\n",
    "      else \"→ Los síntomas generales no mejoran significativamente el ajuste\")\n",
    "\n",
    "comparacion.to_csv(OUT_TABLES / \"comparacion_modelos_logisticos.csv\", index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Tabla de OR ajustados y forest plot — Modelo M4 (completo)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# EXTRACCIÓN DE OR AJUSTADOS — MODELO M4\n",
    "# El modelo M4 es el más completo: controla tanto por el perfil clínico\n",
    "# completo (evitando confusión entre síntomas relacionados) como por\n",
    "# características sociodemográficas (sexo, edad, aseguramiento, estrato).\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "modelo_final = modelos[\"M4_completo\"]\n",
    "ic = modelo_final.conf_int()\n",
    "\n",
    "tabla_or = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Variable\":   modelo_final.params.index,\n",
    "    \"OR_ajustado\":  np.exp(modelo_final.params.values).round(3),\n",
    "    \"IC95_inf\":   np.exp(ic[0].values).round(3),\n",
    "    \"IC95_sup\":   np.exp(ic[1].values).round(3),\n",
    "    \"p_valor\":    modelo_final.pvalues.values,\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filtrar solo variables clínicas principales\n",
    "tabla_or_clinicas = tabla_or[\n",
    "    tabla_or[\"Variable\"].isin(todas_clinicas)\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "tabla_or_clinicas[\"p_valor_fmt\"] = tabla_or_clinicas[\"p_valor\"].apply(\n",
    "    lambda x: f\"{x:.3e}\" if x < 0.001 else f\"{x:.3f}\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "tabla_or_clinicas[\"Tipo\"] = [\n",
    "    \"Signo de alarma\" if v in SIGNOS_ALARMA else \"Síntoma general\"\n",
    "    for v in tabla_or_clinicas[\"Variable\"]\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"OR ajustados — Modelo M4 (completo):\")\n",
    "display(tabla_or_clinicas.sort_values(\"OR_ajustado\", ascending=False))\n",
    "tabla_or_clinicas.to_csv(OUT_TABLES / \"OR_ajustados_M4_DCSA.csv\", index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# FOREST PLOT — OR AJUSTADOS (MODELO M4)\n",
    "# Este es el gráfico central del análisis clínico explicativo.\n",
    "# Muestra la asociación INDEPENDIENTE de cada manifestación clínica\n",
    "# con la hospitalización, controlando por todas las demás.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "df_fp = tabla_or_clinicas.sort_values(\"OR_ajustado\").copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 8))\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, (_, fila) in enumerate(df_fp.iterrows()):\n",
    "    color = COLORS[\"con_signos\"] if fila[\"Tipo\"] == \"Signo de alarma\" else COLORS[\"sin_signos\"]\n",
    "    sig   = fila[\"p_valor\"] < 0.05\n",
    "    marker = \"D\" if sig else \"o\"\n",
    "    size   = 10 if sig else 7\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.errorbar(\n",
    "        x=fila[\"OR_ajustado\"], y=i,\n",
    "        xerr=[[fila[\"OR_ajustado\"] - fila[\"IC95_inf\"]],\n",
    "              [fila[\"IC95_sup\"] - fila[\"OR_ajustado\"]]],\n",
    "        fmt=marker, capsize=5, markersize=size,\n",
    "        color=color, elinewidth=1.8,\n",
    "        markeredgecolor=\"white\", markeredgewidth=0.8\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.text(\n",
    "        fila[\"IC95_sup\"] + 0.07, i,\n",
    "        f\"{fila['OR_ajustado']:.2f}\\n[{fila['IC95_inf']:.2f}–{fila['IC95_sup']:.2f}]\",\n",
    "        va=\"center\", fontsize=8, color=\"#333333\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_yticks(range(len(df_fp)))\n",
    "ax.set_yticklabels(df_fp[\"Variable\"], fontsize=10)\n",
    "ax.axvline(1, color=COLORS[\"neutral\"], linestyle=\"--\", linewidth=1.5)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Odds Ratio ajustado (IC 95%)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\n",
    "    \"Forest plot — OR ajustados por manifestaciones clínicas y variables sociodemográficas\\n\"\n",
    "    \"Dengue con signos de alarma — Bucaramanga\",\n",
    "    fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlim(0, df_fp[\"IC95_sup\"].max() + 1.2)\n",
    "\n",
    "leyenda = [\n",
    "    mpatches.Patch(color=COLORS[\"con_signos\"], label=\"Signo de alarma\"),\n",
    "    mpatches.Patch(color=COLORS[\"sin_signos\"], label=\"Síntoma general\"),\n",
    "    plt.Line2D([0], [0], marker=\"D\", color=\"gray\", markersize=8, linewidth=0, label=\"p < 0.05\"),\n",
    "    plt.Line2D([0], [0], marker=\"o\", color=\"gray\", markersize=7, linewidth=0, label=\"p ≥ 0.05\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "ax.legend(handles=leyenda, fontsize=9, loc=\"lower right\")\n",
    "ax.grid(axis=\"x\", alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.savefig(OUT_FIGURES / \"07_forest_plot_OR_ajustados_M4.png\",\n",
    "            dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\", facecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print(\"✅ Forest plot de OR ajustados guardado\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Análisis de VIF (colinealidad)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# VARIANCE INFLATION FACTOR (VIF)\n",
    "# Un VIF > 5 indica colinealidad moderada; > 10 es problemático.\n",
    "# En modelos explicativos la colinealidad infla los errores estándar\n",
    "# y hace inestables las estimaciones individuales de OR.\n",
    "# En modelos predictivos (notebook 03) la colinealidad es menos crítica.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "X_matrix = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    modelo_final.model.exog,\n",
    "    columns=modelo_final.model.exog_names\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "vif_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Variable\": X_matrix.columns,\n",
    "    \"VIF\": [variance_inflation_factor(X_matrix.values, i)\n",
    "            for i in range(X_matrix.shape[1])]\n",
    "})\n",
    "vif_df = (\n",
    "    vif_df[vif_df[\"Variable\"] != \"Intercept\"]\n",
    "    .sort_values(\"VIF\", ascending=False)\n",
    "    .reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    ")\n",
    "vif_df[\"Nivel_colinealidad\"] = pd.cut(\n",
    "    vif_df[\"VIF\"],\n",
    "    bins=[0, 5, 10, float(\"inf\")],\n",
    "    labels=[\"Bajo (<5)\", \"Moderado (5–10)\", \"Alto (>10)\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(vif_df.head(20))\n",
    "vif_df.to_csv(OUT_TABLES / \"VIF_modelo_M4.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "print(\"\\nVariables con VIF alto (>5):\")\n",
    "display(vif_df[vif_df[\"VIF\"] > 5])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
